 "story": {
  "title": "The ice sheet's summer",
  "lede": "East of Kangerlussuaq the Greenland ice sheet meets the tundra. NISAR watched its melt zone from June to October.",
  "body": [
   "Over ice, NISAR listens with one channel, HH. Wet snow absorbs the radar. As the summer goes on, rough bare ice and refrozen crust send more of it back.",
   "Across the ice in this box, HH rose 4 to 5 dB at the height of summer, peaking on the August 19 pass, and settled back by October. The tundra to the west barely moved."
